Adam Trace Spragg <spragg@pc5.cs.ucdavis.edu> wrote:

> Is there a semi-official list of conducts, both specifically in-game as well
> as made up by players?  What are the requirements of each conduct?
> 
> For instance, I don't know what the "illiterate" conduct actually implies,
> and have seen lots of questions as to the specifics...

For the officially-recognized conducts, you can find a list and the
requirements in several places, including:

http://www.nethack.org/v343/Guidebook.html#_TOCentry_38

Example from the Guidebook:

An illiterate character cannot read or write. This includes reading a
scroll, spellbook, fortune cookie message, or t-shirt; writing a scroll;
or making an engraving of anything other than a single ``x'' (the
traditional signature of an illiterate person). Reading an engraving, or
any item that is absolutely necessary to win the game, is not counted
against this conduct. The identity of scrolls and spellbooks (and
knowledge of spells) in your starting inventory is assumed to be learned
from your teachers prior to the start of the game and isn't counted. 
